---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../i18n/meta";
import { SITE_URL as siteUrl } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbLd } from "../lib/breadcrumbs";
import { ogImageFor } from "../lib/og";

const m = meta.en.privacy;

const pageLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: m.title,
  description: m.description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  url: new URL("/privacy", siteUrl).toString(),
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website` },
};
---

<Layout
  title={m.title}
  description={m.description}
  ogImage={ogImageFor("/privacy")}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd("en", [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy" },
  ]), pageLd]}
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">Last updated: 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser soccer game. It is a fantasy
        soccer world cup draft simulator. This Privacy Policy explains what we
        collect. It explains how we use it. It explains your choices. It covers the
        soccer simulator, the football draft simulator and every page of the world
        cup fantasy game. That includes the teams index, the how-to-play guide and
        the draft tool.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app runs in your browser. No account. No download. So the data is
        small. We kept this policy short where we can. By using the site you agree
        to these practices. If anything is unclear, reach us on the contact page.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">1. Overview</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          World Cup Draft Simulator respects your privacy. This policy explains
          how. It covers the whole fantasy football world cup experience. That is
          the soccer simulator you play. The football draft simulator that builds
          your XI. The teams index you scout. The how-to-play guide you read. It
          says what we collect. It says how we use it. It says your controls.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We are a free browser soccer game. No subscription. No account. You open
          the online soccer game. You play. We collect only what we need. By using
          the site you agree. If we change the rules, we post the update here.
          This policy is not a contract. But it is our promise to treat your visit
          with care. Where local law is stronger, that law applies. We keep
          collection small. We do not sell data. You can clear everything in a few
          clicks.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We built a soccer game with no download so you can play between matches.
          We keep your visit as private as the game is free.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This is a browser game. That shapes what we collect. We do not need an
          account. We do not collect your name, email or payment to play. The
          world cup simulator has no sign-up. No purchases. Your game state stays
          in your browser. That is your draft, your squad, your formation, your
          results and your saved cups. It is not sent to our servers.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          So the soccer simulator is private by design. It lives on your device.
          Closing the tab or clearing storage removes it. We may also collect basic
          technical data. Your IP, browser, device and pages visited. This helps
          us see how the football draft simulator is used. The data is grouped. It
          does not tell us who you are. We do not build a profile from your
          drafts.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Because the app is a free browser soccer game with no download, only
          routine analytics leave your device. They show which features you use.
          If you do not want that, turn off analytics cookies. The interactive
          soccer simulator still works. Every match is computed on your machine.
          In short, we collect only what keeps the fantasy soccer draft running and
          helps us improve it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may use cookies to remember settings and to measure use. Third-party
          analytics may use cookies too. They count how many people open the
          soccer simulator. They show which football formations are drafted most.
          They show if the teams index helps. Cookies are not needed to play. The
          world cup simulation runs on your device. But they help us choose what
          to improve.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can turn off cookies any time. The browser soccer game still works.
          You only lose the anonymous signal we use to plan. We do not use ad
          cookies. We do not run ad networks on this fantasy soccer draft site. So
          there is no cross-site tracking. If you came as a soccer draft game, a
          free soccer simulation game or an interactive soccer simulator, expect a
          clean, ad-light place. Some browsers send "Do Not Track". We honour it
          where we can.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Because this is a soccer game with no download, no software phones home.
          Only the page load and, if on, anonymous analytics. We review our cookies
          often and drop what we no longer need. We keep the world cup fantasy game
          light and respectful of your settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">4. How we use information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We use the data to run and improve the site. We see how visitors use
          the game. We fix bugs. We make the soccer simulator faster. We check
          that every football formation drafts right. We confirm the penalty
          shootout simulator is fair on real devices. We look at group trends,
          not single drafts. That tells us which old squads to add. It tells us if
          the world cup simulation feels balanced.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not sell your data. We do not rent it. We do not share it for ads.
          The fantasy soccer draft you build stays on your device. Only anonymous
          analytics reach us. We also use the data to keep the service safe. We
          spot odd traffic. We stop abuse. We keep the free browser soccer game
          online during a real tournament. None of this needs to know who you are.
          The app has no account. No download. You stay unknown while you play.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If a change needs more data, we ask first. A world cup simulator built
          on trust does not quietly take more. The goal is a smoother, fairer
          interactive soccer simulator. We do not target you elsewhere. We do not
          build shadow profiles from your drafts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">5. Data sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not share your data with others except in narrow cases. We may
          share with helpers who run the site. An analytics or hosting partner.
          They must keep it secret. They may use it only for that job. We may
          share if the law requires it. For a valid legal request. Or to protect
          the site and its users.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The soccer simulator stores your draft on your device. So there is
          normally nothing to share. We never received your tournament. The
          grouped analytics we hold may go to a measurement partner. But it is not
          sold. It does not name you. We will not sell the site in a way that
          breaks this policy. If the world cup fantasy game changes owner, we tell
          users. Our promises stay. We do not share with advertisers. The football
          draft simulator has no ad network. No cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          In practice, the only sharing is quiet help that keeps the free browser
          soccer game online. Even then, your rosters and cups never leave your
          device. A world cup simulator should feel like a private playground. Our
          rules keep the interactive soccer simulator that way. Whether you found
          it as a soccer draft game, a free soccer simulation game, or the easiest
          online soccer game to open on a phone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">6. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The site is not for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
          their data. The soccer simulator needs no account. No sign-up. A child
          can open the world cup fantasy game and play. They give us no name or
          email. That keeps risk low by design. We do not ask age to play. We do
          not force sign-up. If a parent thinks a child under 13 sent us data by
          email, we delete it fast.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The content comes from World Cup history. It suits fans of any age.
          Many families use the interactive soccer simulator to learn the greatest
          world cup teams. We still suggest younger players use the free browser
          soccer game with a parent. The squads are editorial, not official. If
          your region sets a different age for consent, that age applies. Our aim
          is simple. A soccer game with no download that families can enjoy. The
          fantasy soccer draft collects almost nothing. The online soccer game is
          as friendly as its gameplay.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">7. Your choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can clear your game data any time. Clear your browser storage for
          the site. That removes your drafts, squads and cups. You can also turn
          off cookie tracking. Use your browser settings. Or the analytics
          opt-out. The soccer simulator keeps everything local. Clearing storage
          is a full reset. There is no server copy to fix.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can block or delete cookies. You can turn on "Do Not Track". You can
          use a privacy tool. The football draft simulator still runs. All matches
          are on your device. Your local law may give more rights. To see, fix or
          delete data we hold. Or to object to its use. Contact us through the
          contact page. We answer in the time the law sets. We will not punish you
          for asking.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The world cup fantasy game makes these choices easy. No account to
          close. No download to remove. Open the online soccer game. Play as much
          as you like. Clear it in seconds when done. A world cup simulator should
          give you control. On the pitch and over your data. This policy is where
          we promise that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this policy as the soccer simulator grows. We post
          changes on this page. The "Last updated" date shows when. If a change is
          big — like collecting more than anonymous analytics — we say so clearly.
          Where the law requires, we ask before it starts. Small changes may
          happen without notice. A wording fix. Or a new storage method in the
          football draft simulator. We suggest you check back now and then.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This matters if you use the world cup fantasy game for a class or a
          community. The spirit stays the same. The free browser soccer game
          collects little. Sells nothing. Keeps your drafts on your device. If you
          disagree with an update, your fix is simple. Stop using the site. Clear
          your storage. No account to close. No download to remove. The
          interactive soccer simulator should stay trusted as it grows.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Whether we add more old squads, deeper football formations or a richer
          penalty shootout simulator. However you found us — as a soccer draft
          game, a free soccer simulation game, or the easiest online soccer game to
          open between matches — this policy explains our side. The "Last updated"
          line shows when it last changed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">9. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions about this policy? Or about how the soccer simulator handles
          data? We can help. The fastest way is the contact page. Write to us
          about anything. A cookie setting. Or a feature idea for the football
          draft simulator. The world cup fantasy game stores your drafts locally.
          So most "delete my data" questions are solved by clearing storage. But
          if we hold anything — like analytics choices — we act fast.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We welcome notes from parents, teachers and group leaders. They use the
          free browser soccer game in class or on match day. They want to know what
          stays on device. You can reach us whether you found the app as a soccer
          draft game, a free soccer simulation game or an interactive soccer
          simulator. We read every message, even during a real tournament.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Privacy is not a one-time box for a world cup simulator. It is a promise.
          The contact page keeps that promise. If something here is unclear, tell
          us in plain words. We will explain it plainly. <a
            class="text-mint underline" href="/contact">Contact us</a> and help
          keep the online soccer game as careful with your data as it is free to
          play.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
